}\]
The remaining unlabeled map is induced by the map 
\[
  \coprod_{a\in \scr{A}}\scr{C}(F(a), K(F(a)))\to \coprod_{c\in \scr{C}}\scr{C}(c, K(c)).
\]

For a functor  $F\colon \scr{A}\to \scr{C}$, a right dualizable $(\scr{C},\scr{D})$-bimodule $\scr{M}$, 
an object $a\in \scr{A}$ and a map of $(1_\scr{V},1_\scr{V})$-{bimodules} 
 $\alpha \colon 1_\scr{V}\to {_{I_a}\scr{A}_{I_a}}$
the trace of 
\[1_\scr{V}\odot {_{F\circ I_a}\scr{M}}\xrightarrow{\alpha \odot \id_{{_{F\circ I_a}\scr{M}}}} 
{_{I_a}\scr{A}_{I_a}}\odot {_{F\circ I_a}\scr{M}}
\cong 
{_{I_a}\scr{A}_{I_a}}\odot {_{I_a}({_{F}\scr{M}})}
\xrightarrow{\rbmm{\epsilon}{I_a}{\scr{A}}{U_\scr{A}}{_F\scr{M}}}
 {_{I_a}({_{F}\scr{M}})}\cong {_{F\circ I_a} \scr{M}}\]
as a map of $(1_{\scr{V}},\scr{D})$-bimodules is 
\[{1_\scr{V}\xrightarrow\alpha
\sh{{_{I_a}\scr{A}_{I_a}}}\xrightarrow{\tr(\rbm{\epsilon}{I_a}{\scr{B}}{U_\scr{D}})}
\sh{\scr{A}}\xrightarrow{\chi(_F\scr{M})} \sh{\scr{D}}.
}\]

