\end{align*} 

\begin{example} 
We now return to the example at the beginning of this subsection.  Let $C$ and $D$ be rings, $Q$ be an $(C,C)$-bimodule, $P$ be an $(D,D)$-bimodule, $M$ be an $(C,D)$-bimodule that is finitely generated and projective as an right $D$-module, and let $f\colon Q\otimes_C M\to M\otimes_D P$ be a homomorphism. 

\cref{ex:base_change_and_natural_transformation} with the  substitutions 
