&$C$
&$\Mod_D^c$
&$D$
&${-\otimes_CQ}$
&${-\otimes_DP}$
&${-\otimes_CM}$
&$-\otimes_Cf$
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
implies the bottom square in the following diagram commutes.
\[\xymatrix{
  \sh{Q}	\ar[d]	\ar[rr]^-{\tr(f)}
  &&\sh{P}\ar[d]
  \\
  \sh{\Mod_C^c(C,Q)}
	\ar[d]
	\ar[rr]^-{\tr(f_*)}
  &&\sh{\Mod_D^c(D,P)}\ar[d]
  \\
  \sh{(\Mod_C^c)_{-\otimes_CQ}}\ar[r]^-{\sh{\psi}}
  &\sh{_{-\otimes_CM}(\Mod_D^c)_{-\otimes_CM\otimes_DP}}\ar[r]
